    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The canyon sits at an elevation of 1,024 feet (312 m) in the Sierra Nevada foothills.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Butte_Creek_Canyon%2C_California"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "A 287‑acre ecological reserve protects two units—Virgin Valley and Canyon—along Butte Creek, preserving riparian forests of Great Valley Oak and Cottonwood.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16,
        17,
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://wildlife.ca.gov/Lands/Places-to-Visit/Butte-Creek-Canyon-ER"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Wildlife in the reserve includes wintering bald eagles, western pond turtles, and red‑legged frogs, alongside deer, coyotes, and bobcats.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        19
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://wildlife.ca.gov/Lands/Places-to-Visit/Butte-Creek-Canyon-ER"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Before state acquisition, the canyon floor was dominated by mining from the 1850s, which altered the landscape and prompted the reserve’s creation.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        25,
        26,
        27
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://wildlife.ca.gov/Lands/Places-to-Visit/Butte-Creek-Canyon-ER"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Designated as an ecological reserve in 1988, the area now offers hiking, birdwatching, and limited fishing while protecting anadromous fish habitats.",
